  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday) \nIssued at 1002 PM CDT Fri Sep 4 2026\n\nBeginning on Sunday, the center of the upper level ridge is progged \nto position nearly directly overhead, which will keep precipitation \nchances at zero through at least the middle of next week. \nTemperatures will also remain well above normal during this period \nwith daily highs hovering in the 95-100F range, although we \ncurrently expect to remain a few degrees below record-breaking \nlevels. The evolution of the ridging aloft becomes more uncertain \nWednesday and beyond, with some solutions hinting at a northward \nretreat of the ridge axis which could re-introduce some low storm \nchances by the end of next week.",
